  "observations": [
    {
      "topic": "issuance",
      "result": "Human owner with fresh write role, or human effective engine administrator for another fresh writer owner, may issue. Automation actors are refused. Serialized accountLock transaction captures current owner sessionVersion; finite future expiry max30days, valid name, 1..32 explicit mount scopes and valid deny-aware rule action/path metadata. Identity row stores hash only; issued credential is returned once in operation result.",
      "source": "kv-registry.ts:294-312; kv-schemas.ts:24; kv-credentials.ts:1-17"
    },
    {
      "topic": "credential audience and projection",
      "result": "32 random bytes and UUID4 produce distinct opaque KV credential. Exact Bearer grammar and timingSafeEqual SHA256 hash comparison; automation route authenticates Authorization before body/dispatch and does not consult human cookies. Middleware exempts exact automation path. List projection excludes hash and credential; secretResponse marks replies private/no-store.",
      "source": "kv-credentials.ts; automation/route.ts; kv-registry.ts:315-329; middleware.ts:6-19; secret-http.ts:4-13"
    },
    {
      "topic": "current identity and owner",
      "result": "current() rereads owner and identity; absent owner, actor/owner sessionVersion mismatch, wrong owner, recorded ownerSessionVersion mismatch, revokedAt, expiresAt<=Date.now or current nonwrite role deny. authenticateIdentity invokes current() after hash verification; authorize invokes current() again and intersects fresh user and identity rules. Engine administration categorically refuses automation actors.",
      "source": "kv-registry.ts:37-73;315-322"
    },
    {
      "topic": "revocation and reset semantics",
      "result": "Revoke is serialized and permits only a fresh human writer owner or effective administrator, writes revokedAt and audit atomically. Repeated DELETE updates timestamp; no unrevocation method here. PasswordHash updates increment sessionVersion, thereby invalidating prior identities without rewriting rows. Owner deletion denies through absent current owner, not a claimed identity cascade.",
      "source": "kv-registry.ts:332-339; account-store.ts:74-109"
    },
    {
      "topic": "demotion semantics",
      "result": "Demotion denies authority while owner role is readonly, using fresh role checks on every current()/authorize() call. account-store increments sessionVersion only for passwordHash, not role change. Source does not durably mark identity revoked on demotion; later re-promotion could restore still-unexpired/nonrevoked token authority subject to fresh policies. No permanent invalidation or revokedAt stamping is claimed, and preserved current-owner privilege contract supplies no supported basis for changing this behavior.",
      "source": "account-store.ts:89-92; kv-registry.ts:37-44; docs/SECRETS-ENGINE.md:130"
    },
    {
      "topic": "native dispatch authorization",
      "result": "Selected read path authorizes before native access and again in serialized metadata-audit transaction before value release. Selected change path uses permitted(), start()/fresh() and fresh() immediately before canonical replacement. This is source tracing, not a proof of atomic authorization across an external native network operation, all dispatch branches or runtime effects.",
      "source": "kv-native-engine.ts:26-38;59-72;92-106;148-157;232-244"
    },
